WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:01.735
Welcome back.

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.502
President Biden

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.203
is calling out

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.305
Elon Musk saying the billionaire

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.240
bought a social media platform

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.776
that, quote, spews lies across the world.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:10.744
And, quote,

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:11.811
The president's remarks

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:12.612
follow news

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:13.313
that Twitter

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.814
laid off thousands of employees,

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.983
including 15% of its trust

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.585
and safety workforce.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.886
Just a week after

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.888
it was acquired by Musk.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.757
CNN tech reporter Brian Fung

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:24.858
is following the story for us.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:27.193
So, Brian, good to see you.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.895
Let's talk about these massive cuts.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:29.262
I mean,

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.663
and they come just days

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.132
before the midterms.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.533
In fact, civil rights groups

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.267
say it could

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.369
jeopardize the platform's ability

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.571
to safeguard the democratic process.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.639
Is Twitter

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.940
Is there anybody left at Twitter

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.876
to even respond to the critics?

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.544
Well, Fred, Twitter is saying

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:45.612
that it's still committed

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.147
to protecting the election

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.082
and that none of its content moderation

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.350
policies have changed.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.484
But as you pointed out,

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.585
civil rights groups

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.421
and leaders are saying that

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.822
even though Twitter

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:56.489
may still have

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.857
these policies on the books,

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.993
the layoffs could make it harder for them

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.861
to enforce the policies

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.329
that it does have.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.698
Meanwhile, you have major advertisers

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.500
pulling out of

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.636
spending on Twitter advertising,

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.971
and that's caused sharp declines

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.673
in revenue at Twitter,

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.708
according to Elon Musk.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.743
And, you know,

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.477
to shore up

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.344
revenue, Musk

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.980
has this kind of harebrained plan to

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.983
charge people for verification,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.818
to have that little blue

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.986
checkmark next to their accounts,

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.988
which some experts have said

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.357
could have unintended consequences

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.725
if it's rolled out

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.027
in the post-election period

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.029
or even before the election, potentially

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.932
without proper testing.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.401
You could potentially see, for example,

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:41.768
you know,

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.302
some people

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.970
paying to have that blue checkmark

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.338
and then changing their names

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:48.241
to impersonate official accounts or

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:51.077
or try to spread misinformation

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.812
under a verified account.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.948
And how would the company respond to that

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.850
with a smaller workforce?

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.084
It's unclear.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.385
Twitter, of course,

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.053
laid off

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.554
15% of its

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.522
trust and safety team,

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.890
but 50%

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.258
of its overall workforce

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.726
amounting to about

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:10.930
3700 people across the overall company.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.599
All of this, of course, coming

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.634
just days before the election,

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.669
injecting further uncertainty

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.372
into an already chaotic situation Fred.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.006
And Brian,

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:20.640
I think a lot of us

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.841
have been reading

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.110
all about what a lot of former

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.745
Twitter employees have been saying.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.448
But now what about the former CEO?

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.983
How, you know,

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:30.984
what kind of reaction

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.852
is coming from the former CEO?

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:33.153
Yes.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.020
Well, Jack Dorsey,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.288
the former CEO of Twitter,

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.490
just tweeted about a half hour ago

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:39.159
Let me read what he said.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.560
He said, Folks at Twitter, past

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.529
and present are strong and resilient.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:43.696
They will always find a way,

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.298
no matter how difficult the moment.

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:47.200
I realize many are angry with me.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.668
I own the responsibility for

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.904
why everyone is in this situation.

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.839
I grew the company size too quickly.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:53.940
I apologize for that.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.441
Very interesting tweet

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.110
from from Jack Dorsey's

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.178
taking accountability or

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:59.913
responsibility for having

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:01.881
grown the company

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:02.749
too large

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.150
and thus putting the company

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:04.751
in a position

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.519
where layoffs may have been necessary.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.388
But not really addressing

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.589
some of the other

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.458
election security or election

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.960
integrity questions

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.295
that are swirling around Twitter

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.030
at this time.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.731
That's a very sensitive time, Fred.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.000
Yeah, a remarkable sequence of events.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.902
Brian Fong, thanks so much.

